@page
@inject IOptions<ShopOptions> Shop
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of purchase"; var s = Shop.Value; }
<div class="prose">
    <partial name="_DraftNotice" />
    <h1>Terms of purchase</h1>
    <p>These terms apply when you buy from @s.Name. <em>[Company name, organisation number and address go here.]</em></p>
    <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
    <p>All prices are in Swedish kronor (SEK) and include 25% VAT. Shipping costs are shown in the cart before you pay. Card payments are handled by SumUp, and we never see or store your card details.</p>
    <h2>Delivery</h2>
    <p>We ship within Sweden. Items in stock are usually sent within <em>[X]</em> working days. Items printed to order may take longer, and we'll tell you if so.</p>
    <h2>Right of withdrawal</h2>
    <p>You have 14 days to change your mind about shop items. See <a asp-page="/Info/Returns">Returns &amp; right of withdrawal</a>. Custom-made items are exempt.</p>
    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If an item arrives faulty or damaged, contact us at <a href="mailto:@s.ContactEmail">@s.ContactEmail</a> and we'll make it right. You have the right to complain about faults for three years under the Swedish Consumer Sales Act (konsumentköplagen).</p>
    <h2>Disputes</h2>
    <p>If we can't agree, you can turn to the National Board for Consumer Disputes (Allmänna reklamationsnämnden, arn.se) or the EU's online dispute resolution platform.</p>
</div>
